  ],
  "core_idea": "Coding standards describe how an agent behaves when it writes code, so they are behaviour policies, and their strength is describing intent rather than tool settings. Our own standards, measured by coding.sgit.ai, are 31 rules kept mostly by habit with no passing CI guard: a mandate with no barrier. Fractal semantic graphs connect a codebase from intent to stories, features, classes and methods, so common intents can keep several teams and languages aligned on one feature, and language models make those mappings affordable while people and tests confirm them.",
